// - `write_<name>` writes a reply into a buffer the caller owns. A buffer too
//   small is an error and nothing is written.
// - `MAX_BODY_BYTES` and `<NAME>_MAX_BODY_BYTES` are the largest a reply body can
//   be, which a host sizes its response buffers from.
//
// Replies carry the values the host holds at run time; the deploy fixes only
// their fields, types and bounds. A value outside a bound is refused and never
// written, so the sizes above hold for every reply this module writes.

